Package: sediros-firstboot
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: @SEDIROS_ARCH@
Maintainer: The SedirOS Authors <ahmetatakan.tech@gmail.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, openssh-server, openssh-client, util-linux, fdisk, e2fsprogs, hostname, systemd
Description: First-boot setup of SedirOS cloud images
 For SedirOS images on cloud and VPS providers. On the first boot of each
 new instance (a new instance id, also after cloning a disk) it creates new
 SSH host keys, sets the hostname, adds the admin user's SSH keys and grows
 the root file system to the disk, from the provider's metadata: a NoCloud
 seed (label cidata) or the EC2-style service at 169.254.169.254.
 .
 User-data scripts are never run: SedirOS does not execute code from the
 provider's control panel as root. From #cloud-config only hostname and
 ssh_authorized_keys are used; anything else is reported at login.
